error[E0322]: `distinct` types need a name
  --> tests/ui/type_args.wid:11:16
   |
11 |   puts size_of(distinct Int)
   |                ^^^^^^^^^^^^ a `distinct` type is declared once, as a constant
   = note: each `distinct` declaration creates a new type, so an unnamed one could never match another
help: declare it at package level, like `Meters = distinct Int`, then use `Meters`
   = see `wid explain E0322`

error[E0319]: `block(…)` types only describe `&block` parameters
  --> tests/ui/type_args.wid:12:17
   |
12 |   puts align_of(block(Int))
   |                 ^^^^^^^^^^ a block cannot be stored or passed as a value
help: for a storable callback, use a `proc(…)` type
   = see `wid explain E0319`

error[E0105]: `export` is not a proc type attribute
  --> tests/ui/type_args.wid:13:18
   |
13 |   puts size_of(@[export] proc(Int))
   |                  ^^^^^^ proc types only take `c`, as in `@[c] proc(C.int)`
   = see `wid explain E0105`

error[E0301]: optional of an optional
  --> tests/ui/type_args.wid:14:16
   |
14 |   puts size_of(Int??)
   |                ^^^^^ `T??` is the same as `T?`
   = see `wid explain E0301`

error[E0105]: a `?` after a space starts a conditional
  --> tests/ui/type_args.wid:15:20
   |
15 |   puts size_of(Int ?)
   |                    ^ this reads as `cond ? a : b`, which needs both values
help: for an optional type, write the `?` right after the type
   |   puts size_of(Int?)
   = see `wid explain E0105`

error[E0105]: a `?` after a space starts a conditional
  --> tests/ui/type_args.wid:16:31
   |
16 |   puts type_info(Pool(Int, 2) ?).name
   |                               ^ this reads as `cond ? a : b`, which needs both values
help: for an optional type, write the `?` right after the type
   |   puts type_info(Pool(Int, 2)?).name
   = see `wid explain E0105`

error[E0322]: `count` is a variable, not a type
